{"title":"Career Roadmap · QC/QA Analyst","role":"QC/QA Analyst","summary":"A QC/QA Analyst in the pharmaceutical industry works to ensure that medicines, raw materials, manufacturing processes, laboratory results, and documentation meet established quality, safety, identity, purity, strength, and regulatory requirements.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Pharm (Bachelor of Pharmacy)","Course":"Pharmaceutical Sciences"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A QC/QA Analyst in the pharmaceutical industry works to ensure that medicines, raw materials, manufacturing processes, laboratory results, and documentation meet established quality, safety, identity, purity, strength, and regulatory requirements."},{"type":"p","text":"The two functions are closely related but different:"},{"type":"h","text":"Quality Control — QC"},{"type":"p","text":"Focuses primarily on testing and analytical verification."},{"type":"h","text":"Sample"},{"type":"h","text":"Testing"},{"type":"h","text":"Analytical Results"},{"type":"h","text":"Specification Comparison"},{"type":"h","text":"Pass / Fail / Investigation"},{"type":"h","text":"Quality Assurance — QA"},{"type":"p","text":"Focuses primarily on systems, processes, compliance, and prevention of quality failures."},{"type":"h","text":"Quality System"},{"type":"h","text":"SOPs"},{"type":"h","text":"Process Controls"},{"type":"h","text":"Documentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Audit / Monitoring"},{"type":"h","text":"Deviation / CAPA"},{"type":"h","text":"Continuous Improvement"},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Pharm graduate can build a strong entry-level profile by developing expertise in pharmaceutical analysis + GMP + documentation + laboratory systems + regulatory compliance."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"B.Pharm"},{"type":"h","text":"Industrial Training / Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"QC / QA Trainee"},{"type":"h","te